# nix-direnv watches .envrc, flake.nix and flake.lock, and nothing else. An edit
# to nix/bevy-shell.nix therefore does NOT invalidate the cached shell: direnv
# goes on serving the old one, and the cache file even carries a fresh mtime, so
# it looks current. That is how a corrected devShell can keep exporting the
# SDKROOT it was corrected to stop exporting. Watch the file explicitly.
watch_file nix/bevy-shell.nix

use flake
